<section class="wp-block-fur-accordion js-accordion alignfull fur-bg-parchment">
    <div class="fur-container">
        
<header class="fur-border-t-[3px] fur-border-orange fur-pt-[3px] fur-py-14 fur-flex fur-flex-col fur-gap-y-8 before:fur-content-[''] before:fur-block before:fur-w-full before:fur-h-[1px] before:fur-bg-orange ">
    
            <h2 class="fur-title--heading-2 fur-text-purple fur-max-w-[900px] ">
            Learn More About CoreData.nyc        </h2>
    
            <p class="fur-body--lg fur-text-black fur-max-w-[900px] ">
            Find detailed information about CoreData.nyc, including how to get started using our  tool and view our data.        </p>
    
    
    </header>


        <div class="fur-flex fur-flex-col fur-gap-4">
            
<div class="js-accordion-item fur-bg-peach">
    <button
        class="js-accordion-toggle fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-between fur-w-full fur-text-left fur-cursor-pointer fur-bg-peach fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-py-6 fur-text-purple hover:fur-text-white hover:fur-bg-purple fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200 fur-group/accordion-item fur-gap-8"
        aria-expanded="false"
    >
        <span class="fur-title--heading-5">
            How to Find The Data        </span>

        <span class="fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-center fur-w-[46px] fur-h-[46px] fur-shrink-0 fur-rounded-full fur-border fur-border-purple fur-text-purple group-hover/accordion-item:fur-border-white group-hover/accordion-item:fur-text-white fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200">
            <svg class="js-accordion-caret fur-w-4 fur-h-4 fur-transition-transform fur-duration-300"
  viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <path d="M8 0V16M0 8H16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
</svg>        </span>
    </button>

    <div class="js-accordion-content fur-overflow-hidden" style="max-height: 0;">
        <div class="fur-py-6 fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-flex fur-flex-col fur-gap-8 fur-border-t fur-border-t-[1px] fur-border-solid fur-border-purple">
                            <div class="wysiwyg-content fur-body--sm fur-text-black fur-max-w-[840px]">
                    <p><span style="font-weight: 400">There are two ways to search for data in CoreData.nyc:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Use the </span><b>Toolbar </b><span style="font-weight: 400">menu across the top of the screen to view and select available datasets.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Search the map by address, location, or BBL (borough-block-lot) with the </span><b>Search Box</b><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Turn map layers on or off, refine a selected dataset, and toggle between Map and Table View with the Control Panel.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The </span><b>Toolbar </b><span style="font-weight: 400">and </span><b>Control Panel</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> work together to help you find the information you are looking for.</span></p>
                </div>

                                    </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="js-accordion-item fur-bg-peach">
    <button
        class="js-accordion-toggle fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-between fur-w-full fur-text-left fur-cursor-pointer fur-bg-peach fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-py-6 fur-text-purple hover:fur-text-white hover:fur-bg-purple fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200 fur-group/accordion-item fur-gap-8"
        aria-expanded="false"
    >
        <span class="fur-title--heading-5">
            Getting Started &#8211; Table View        </span>

        <span class="fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-center fur-w-[46px] fur-h-[46px] fur-shrink-0 fur-rounded-full fur-border fur-border-purple fur-text-purple group-hover/accordion-item:fur-border-white group-hover/accordion-item:fur-text-white fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200">
            <svg class="js-accordion-caret fur-w-4 fur-h-4 fur-transition-transform fur-duration-300"
  viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <path d="M8 0V16M0 8H16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
</svg>        </span>
    </button>

    <div class="js-accordion-content fur-overflow-hidden" style="max-height: 0;">
        <div class="fur-py-6 fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-flex fur-flex-col fur-gap-8 fur-border-t fur-border-t-[1px] fur-border-solid fur-border-purple">
                            <div class="wysiwyg-content fur-body--sm fur-text-black fur-max-w-[840px]">
                    <p><span style="font-weight: 400">View  data  either in  </span><b>Map View</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> or </span><b>Table View</b><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Map View </b><i><span style="font-weight: 400">(default)</span></i><span style="font-weight: 400">: View a map with all of the data shown as either points or regions.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Table View</b><span style="font-weight: 400">: Data can also be displayed as a table. From this view, you may download the data.</span></li>
</ul>
                </div>

                                    </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="js-accordion-item fur-bg-peach">
    <button
        class="js-accordion-toggle fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-between fur-w-full fur-text-left fur-cursor-pointer fur-bg-peach fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-py-6 fur-text-purple hover:fur-text-white hover:fur-bg-purple fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200 fur-group/accordion-item fur-gap-8"
        aria-expanded="false"
    >
        <span class="fur-title--heading-5">
            Selecting Datasets to View on the Map        </span>

        <span class="fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-center fur-w-[46px] fur-h-[46px] fur-shrink-0 fur-rounded-full fur-border fur-border-purple fur-text-purple group-hover/accordion-item:fur-border-white group-hover/accordion-item:fur-text-white fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200">
            <svg class="js-accordion-caret fur-w-4 fur-h-4 fur-transition-transform fur-duration-300"
  viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <path d="M8 0V16M0 8H16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
</svg>        </span>
    </button>

    <div class="js-accordion-content fur-overflow-hidden" style="max-height: 0;">
        <div class="fur-py-6 fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-flex fur-flex-col fur-gap-8 fur-border-t fur-border-t-[1px] fur-border-solid fur-border-purple">
                            <div class="wysiwyg-content fur-body--sm fur-text-black fur-max-w-[840px]">
                    <p><span style="font-weight: 400">The Toolbar allows you to select which datasets you will view on the map. Select from the </span><b>Subsidized Housing Database </b><span style="font-weight: 400">to find specific properties or view sets of subsidized properties by available characteristics.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">There are five other categories on the toolbar called </span><b>Neighborhood Indicators, </b><span style="font-weight: 400">which includes Demographics, Development, Housing, Neighborhood Services and Conditions, and Renters and Rental Conditions. Select an indicator from one of these menus to view on the map or export to a table aggregated at the city, borough, or neighborhood level.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The </span><b>Neighborhood Indicators</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> can be displayed on the map at the same time as property-level information from the Subsidized Housing Database.</span></p>
<p><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-19068" src="https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide2.2_760_570-300x225.png" alt="" width="300" height="225" srcset="https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide2.2_760_570-300x225.png 300w, https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide2.2_760_570.png 760w" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></p>
                </div>

                                    </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="js-accordion-item fur-bg-peach">
    <button
        class="js-accordion-toggle fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-between fur-w-full fur-text-left fur-cursor-pointer fur-bg-peach fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-py-6 fur-text-purple hover:fur-text-white hover:fur-bg-purple fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200 fur-group/accordion-item fur-gap-8"
        aria-expanded="false"
    >
        <span class="fur-title--heading-5">
            Using the Subsidized Housing Database on the Map        </span>

        <span class="fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-center fur-w-[46px] fur-h-[46px] fur-shrink-0 fur-rounded-full fur-border fur-border-purple fur-text-purple group-hover/accordion-item:fur-border-white group-hover/accordion-item:fur-text-white fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200">
            <svg class="js-accordion-caret fur-w-4 fur-h-4 fur-transition-transform fur-duration-300"
  viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <path d="M8 0V16M0 8H16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
</svg>        </span>
    </button>

    <div class="js-accordion-content fur-overflow-hidden" style="max-height: 0;">
        <div class="fur-py-6 fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-flex fur-flex-col fur-gap-8 fur-border-t fur-border-t-[1px] fur-border-solid fur-border-purple">
                            <div class="wysiwyg-content fur-body--sm fur-text-black fur-max-w-[840px]">
                    <ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Use the drop-down menu to filter and browse properties in the five boroughs of New York City that currently receive city, state, or federal subsidies.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">You can refine your search, and thus the properties shown on the map, using the following filters:</span>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>General </b><span style="font-weight: 400">(property characteristics including building size, units, and age)</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Location </b><span style="font-weight: 400">(property location)</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Subsidies </b><span style="font-weight: 400">(properties that have received various types of subsidies)</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Distress </b><span style="font-weight: 400">(properties exhibiting physical or financial distress)</span></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Each property is represented as a dot on the map. Clicking on a dot will bring up a detailed report about that property, also downloadable as a PDF.</span></li>
</ul>
                </div>

                                    </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="js-accordion-item fur-bg-peach">
    <button
        class="js-accordion-toggle fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-between fur-w-full fur-text-left fur-cursor-pointer fur-bg-peach fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-py-6 fur-text-purple hover:fur-text-white hover:fur-bg-purple fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200 fur-group/accordion-item fur-gap-8"
        aria-expanded="false"
    >
        <span class="fur-title--heading-5">
            Using the Neighborhood Indicators on the Map         </span>

        <span class="fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-center fur-w-[46px] fur-h-[46px] fur-shrink-0 fur-rounded-full fur-border fur-border-purple fur-text-purple group-hover/accordion-item:fur-border-white group-hover/accordion-item:fur-text-white fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200">
            <svg class="js-accordion-caret fur-w-4 fur-h-4 fur-transition-transform fur-duration-300"
  viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <path d="M8 0V16M0 8H16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
</svg>        </span>
    </button>

    <div class="js-accordion-content fur-overflow-hidden" style="max-height: 0;">
        <div class="fur-py-6 fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-flex fur-flex-col fur-gap-8 fur-border-t fur-border-t-[1px] fur-border-solid fur-border-purple">
                            <div class="wysiwyg-content fur-body--sm fur-text-black fur-max-w-[840px]">
                    <p><span style="font-weight: 400">These drop-down menus allow you to choose indicators by topic at the city, borough, or neighborhood level pertaining to:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Demographics </b><span style="font-weight: 400">(characteristics of the population, e.g. race and ethnicity, income, place of birth, age, labor market)</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Development </b><span style="font-weight: 400">(density, affordable development, permits)</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Housing </b><span style="font-weight: 400">(sales prices and volume, foreclosure rates, subsidy expirations</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Neighborhood Services and Conditions </b><span style="font-weight: 400"> (school quality, crime rates, commuting characteristics)</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Renters and Rental Conditions</b> (affordability, rent, evictions, subsidies, vacancies</li>
</ul>
                </div>

                                    </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="js-accordion-item fur-bg-peach">
    <button
        class="js-accordion-toggle fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-between fur-w-full fur-text-left fur-cursor-pointer fur-bg-peach fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-py-6 fur-text-purple hover:fur-text-white hover:fur-bg-purple fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200 fur-group/accordion-item fur-gap-8"
        aria-expanded="false"
    >
        <span class="fur-title--heading-5">
            Navigating to Table View        </span>

        <span class="fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-center fur-w-[46px] fur-h-[46px] fur-shrink-0 fur-rounded-full fur-border fur-border-purple fur-text-purple group-hover/accordion-item:fur-border-white group-hover/accordion-item:fur-text-white fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200">
            <svg class="js-accordion-caret fur-w-4 fur-h-4 fur-transition-transform fur-duration-300"
  viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <path d="M8 0V16M0 8H16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
</svg>        </span>
    </button>

    <div class="js-accordion-content fur-overflow-hidden" style="max-height: 0;">
        <div class="fur-py-6 fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-flex fur-flex-col fur-gap-8 fur-border-t fur-border-t-[1px] fur-border-solid fur-border-purple">
                            <div class="wysiwyg-content fur-body--sm fur-text-black fur-max-w-[840px]">
                    <ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Map View and Table View</b><span style="font-weight: 400">: The default display is Map View. To change, select </span><b>Table View</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, as shown below.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b><img decoding="async" class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-19069" src="https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide5_760_570-300x225.png" alt="" width="300" height="225" srcset="https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide5_760_570-300x225.png 300w, https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide5_760_570.png 760w" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></b></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Table View / Tabular Output</b><span style="font-weight: 400">: The datasets available in CoreData.nyc can be exported in a table or list that can be downloaded as a CSV file.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Once you’ve refined your query, click Table View in the upper left hand corner to convert the data displayed on the map into a table.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">You may either download just your query, or the complete subsidy and housing dataset for further analysis.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Export limitations: Please note that </span><b>Table View</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> can only display data pertaining to Subsidized Properties and Neighborhood Indicators. While location-based information is captured in the table, CoreData.nyc cannot generate a Table View of Geographic Boundaries or CoreData Visualizations.</span></li>
</ul>
                </div>

                                    </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="js-accordion-item fur-bg-peach">
    <button
        class="js-accordion-toggle fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-between fur-w-full fur-text-left fur-cursor-pointer fur-bg-peach fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-py-6 fur-text-purple hover:fur-text-white hover:fur-bg-purple fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200 fur-group/accordion-item fur-gap-8"
        aria-expanded="false"
    >
        <span class="fur-title--heading-5">
            Control Panel         </span>

        <span class="fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-center fur-w-[46px] fur-h-[46px] fur-shrink-0 fur-rounded-full fur-border fur-border-purple fur-text-purple group-hover/accordion-item:fur-border-white group-hover/accordion-item:fur-text-white fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200">
            <svg class="js-accordion-caret fur-w-4 fur-h-4 fur-transition-transform fur-duration-300"
  viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <path d="M8 0V16M0 8H16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
</svg>        </span>
    </button>

    <div class="js-accordion-content fur-overflow-hidden" style="max-height: 0;">
        <div class="fur-py-6 fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-flex fur-flex-col fur-gap-8 fur-border-t fur-border-t-[1px] fur-border-solid fur-border-purple">
                            <div class="wysiwyg-content fur-body--sm fur-text-black fur-max-w-[840px]">
                    <p><span style="font-weight: 400">The </span><b>Control Pane</b><span style="font-weight: 400">l is how you control the displayed data. Expand and collapse sections as needed, or toggle a layer switch on or off to show or hide the layer on the map. The layers on the Control Panel are </span><b>Subsidized Properties</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, </span><b>Neighborhood Indicators</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, </span><b>Political and Administrative Geographic Boundaries</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, and </span><b>Floodplain Boundary</b><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-19078" src="https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide2_760_570-300x225.png" alt="" width="300" height="225" srcset="https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide2_760_570-300x225.png 300w, https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide2_760_570.png 760w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></p>
<p><b>Layer &#8211; Subsidized Properties</b><span style="font-weight: 400">: </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">By default when you first load CoreData.nyc the “Subsidized Properties” dataset is activated and the filter “Has Subsidies” is enabled.</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">To apply or change the Subsidized Properties filter, click ‘Subsidized Housing Database’ on the </span><b>Toolbar </b><span style="font-weight: 400">to change the parameters of what properties are displayed.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-19079" src="https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide3_760_570-300x225.png" alt="" width="300" height="225" srcset="https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide3_760_570-300x225.png 300w, https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide3_760_570.png 760w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></p>
<p><b>Layer &#8211; Neighborhood Indicators</b><span style="font-weight: 400">: </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">After you’ve selected a Neighborhood Indicator from the </span><b>Toolbar </b><span style="font-weight: 400">you can further refine the data using the </span><b>Control Panel</b><span style="font-weight: 400">. You can select the </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400">Year </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400">and </span><i><span style="font-weight: 400">Region </span></i><span style="font-weight: 400">for the indicator. Year and region availability varies by indicator; all available options will appear in the drop-down list. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400"> </span><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-19081" src="https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide7_760_570-300x225.png" alt="" width="300" height="225" srcset="https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide7_760_570-300x225.png 300w, https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide7_760_570.png 760w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></p>
<p><b>Layer &#8211; Geographic Boundaries: </b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">You can add an additional geographic boundary to the map. The following boundaries are available from the drop-down list:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Boroughs</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Sub-Borough Areas</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Community Districts</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">City Council Districts</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Congressional Districts</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">State Senate Districts</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">State House Districts</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Troubleshooting: If the data is loading slowly, try turning off one of the datasets by clicking the slider on the Control Panel</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The Geographic Boundaries layer is for visual purposes only. Neighborhood Indicator data cannot be attributed to the boundaries displayed in the Geographic Boundaries layer. To find a Neighborhood Indicator for a specific geography, choose from the Region options in the Control Panel.</span></p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-19082" src="https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide8_760_570-300x225.png" alt="" width="300" height="225" srcset="https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide8_760_570-300x225.png 300w, https://www.furmancenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Slide8_760_570.png 760w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /></p>
                </div>

                                    </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="js-accordion-item fur-bg-peach">
    <button
        class="js-accordion-toggle fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-between fur-w-full fur-text-left fur-cursor-pointer fur-bg-peach fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-py-6 fur-text-purple hover:fur-text-white hover:fur-bg-purple fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200 fur-group/accordion-item fur-gap-8"
        aria-expanded="false"
    >
        <span class="fur-title--heading-5">
            Property Information Sidebar        </span>

        <span class="fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-center fur-w-[46px] fur-h-[46px] fur-shrink-0 fur-rounded-full fur-border fur-border-purple fur-text-purple group-hover/accordion-item:fur-border-white group-hover/accordion-item:fur-text-white fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200">
            <svg class="js-accordion-caret fur-w-4 fur-h-4 fur-transition-transform fur-duration-300"
  viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <path d="M8 0V16M0 8H16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
</svg>        </span>
    </button>

    <div class="js-accordion-content fur-overflow-hidden" style="max-height: 0;">
        <div class="fur-py-6 fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-flex fur-flex-col fur-gap-8 fur-border-t fur-border-t-[1px] fur-border-solid fur-border-purple">
                            <div class="wysiwyg-content fur-body--sm fur-text-black fur-max-w-[840px]">
                    <p><span style="font-weight: 400">Properties in the Subsidized Housing Database are represented as a blue dot on the map. Clicking on the dot will bring up a detailed report (available for download as a PDF) that includes information on:</span></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Property </b><span style="font-weight: 400">(Physical details, ownership, and Department of Finance Assessed Value)</span></li>
<li><b>Political and Administrative Districts</b> (Census Tract, Sub-Borough Area, Districts)</li>
<li><b>Income-Targeted Units</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> (if applicable, income-targeted units by unit size)</span></li>
<li><b>Physical and Financial Condition</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> (housing code violations and tax delinquency)</span></li>
<li><b>Regulatory Tools</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> (regulatory instrument, government agency, start/end date, tenure type)</span></li>
<li><b>City and State Programs </b><span style="font-weight: 400">(name of city or state subsidy program associated with property)</span></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li style="list-style-type: none"></li>
</ul>
                </div>

                                    </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="js-accordion-item fur-bg-peach">
    <button
        class="js-accordion-toggle fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-between fur-w-full fur-text-left fur-cursor-pointer fur-bg-peach fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-py-6 fur-text-purple hover:fur-text-white hover:fur-bg-purple fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200 fur-group/accordion-item fur-gap-8"
        aria-expanded="false"
    >
        <span class="fur-title--heading-5">
            Share a link from CoreData.nyc        </span>

        <span class="fur-flex fur-items-center fur-justify-center fur-w-[46px] fur-h-[46px] fur-shrink-0 fur-rounded-full fur-border fur-border-purple fur-text-purple group-hover/accordion-item:fur-border-white group-hover/accordion-item:fur-text-white fur-transition-colors fur-duration-200">
            <svg class="js-accordion-caret fur-w-4 fur-h-4 fur-transition-transform fur-duration-300"
  viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <path d="M8 0V16M0 8H16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
</svg>        </span>
    </button>

    <div class="js-accordion-content fur-overflow-hidden" style="max-height: 0;">
        <div class="fur-py-6 fur-px-6 lg:fur-px-8 fur-flex fur-flex-col fur-gap-8 fur-border-t fur-border-t-[1px] fur-border-solid fur-border-purple">
                            <div class="wysiwyg-content fur-body--sm fur-text-black fur-max-w-[840px]">
                    <ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Click “Share&#8221;, located on the bottom of the table or map. It will generate a unique link that you can send to a friend or colleague that will take them directly to the map view you have created.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Links are permanent but they may change or become unavailable as the underlying data is updated.</span></li>
</ul>
                </div>

                                    </div>
    </div>
</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>



<section class="wp-block-fur-columns js-columns alignfull fur-bg-parchment">
